    "**ADAM ID: **[sm\\_us7000thcs](https://api.adam.geospatial.wfp.org/api/collections/adam.adam_eq_events/items?uid=sm_us7000thcs) Magnitude 5.6 earthquake at 162.179 depth occurred on Sep 14 2026 43km NW of Daruba. The epicentre of the earthquake was located at latitude 2.4223 longitude 128.1704. It impacted 59928 people within 50km. WFP’s Automated Disaster Analysis and Mapping (ADAM) system is an operational system for collecting, analysing and mapping geospatial and socio-economic information following sudden onset humanitarian emergencies."
